Match the kernel's iommu_dma_cookie layout on 6.14+

The driver allocates NPU IOVAs out of the DMA-IOMMU cookie's iova
domain by casting the kernel-private struct through a local mirror of
its layout. Since 6.14 the MSI cookie is a separate struct and iovad
sits at offset 0; the vendor mirror's leading type enum skews every
field access by 8 bytes, and the first allocation crashes inside
alloc_iova() on a garbage spinlock.

Signed-off-by: Isaiah DeRose-Wilson <isaiahdw@gmail.com>

diff --git a/include/rknpu_iommu.h b/include/rknpu_iommu.h
index 2251766..04c0b82 100644
--- a/include/rknpu_iommu.h
+++ b/include/rknpu_iommu.h
@@ -25,9 +25,17 @@ enum iommu_dma_cookie_type {
 };
 
 struct rknpu_iommu_dma_cookie {
+#if KERNEL_VERSION(6, 14, 0) > LINUX_VERSION_CODE
 	enum iommu_dma_cookie_type type;
-
-	/* Full allocator for IOMMU_DMA_IOVA_COOKIE */
+#endif
+	/*
+	 * Mirrors the head of the kernel's private struct iommu_dma_cookie
+	 * (drivers/iommu/dma-iommu.c). Since 6.14 the MSI cookie is a
+	 * separate struct and iovad sits at offset 0 - with the vendor's
+	 * leading type field the iovad pointer lands 8 bytes into the real
+	 * structure and the first alloc_iova() crashes on a garbage
+	 * spinlock. Only iovad is ever accessed through this cast.
+	 */
 	struct iova_domain iovad;
 };
 
